[agent] ## What I did
[agent] 1. **Loaded all source data** into the pre-provisioned feature groups (all were empty):
[agent]    - `transactions_f35496` ← `transactions.csv` (660) **+** `transactions_late.csv` (68) = 728 rows
[agent]    - `profiles_f35496` (168), `activity_f35496` (1300), `account_health_f35496` (200), `labels_f35496` (100)
[agent] 2. **Created feature view `churntrainingf35496` v1** with `labels_f35496` as the base/spine and LEFT point-in-time joins on `account_id` to the four feature FGs (`churned` as label).
[agent] 3. **Materialized training dataset version 1** (`hops td compute churntrainingf35496 1`) and read it back.
[agent] The point-in-time join is **correct**: 100 rows (one per `labels.csv` row), each feature value is the most recent at/before `label_time`, late transactions included.
[agent] ## What the interface could NOT deliver — the exact column set
[agent] The task requires exactly: `account_id, label_time, amount, balance, credit_score, tier, sessions_7d, health_score, churned`. The materialized TD instead has **16 prefixed columns**:
[agent] ```
[agent] account_id, label_time, churned,
[agent] transactions_f35496_account_id, transactions_f35496_event_time, transactions_f35496_amount, transactions_f35496_balance,
[agent] profiles_f35496_account_id, profiles_f35496_event_time, profiles_f35496_credit_score, profiles_f35496_tier,
[agent] activity_f35496_account_id, activity_f35496_event_time, activity_f35496_sessions_7d,
[agent] account_health_f35496_account_id, account_health_f35496_event_time, account_health_f35496_health_score
[agent] ```
[agent] **Missing CLI capability: per-feature-group feature selection / column projection.** `hops fv create --join` (and `hops fg derive`) always select *all* features from each joined feature group. Because every FG shares the join key `account_id` (and the column `event_time`), hsfs flags ambiguity and **auto-prefixes every feature** of those FGs — so `amount` becomes `transactions_f35496_amount`, and the duplicate `account_id`/`event_time` columns are carried through as extra columns. There is no CLI flag to:
[agent] - select a subset of columns from a joined FG (the SDK's `fg.select([...])`),
[agent] - drop the redundant per-FG `account_id`/`event_time`, or
[agent] - rename output columns.
[agent] I did not work around this locally (blocked, and it would not be a platform artifact). The deliverable `churntrainingf35496` v1 exists on the platform and is point-in-time-correct, but its column **names** cannot be made to match the required exact set through the CLI as it stands.
